From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTOS wireless port <dev@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 19 Oct 2026 16:48:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lwiperf: disable Nagle on the TCP client

The client writes one MSS per tcp_sent callback; with Nagle on and a peer
that delayed-ACKs, that paces the whole measurement at one segment per RTT
(measured: 0.4 Mbit/s on a link whose TX queue was empty 20 s out of 20).
Nagle has no place in a throughput measurement client.

Signed-off-by: RTOS wireless port <dev@example.invalid>
---
diff --git a/src/apps/lwiperf/lwiperf.c b/src/apps/lwiperf/lwiperf.c
index 144c8bd2..65ff7978 100644
--- a/src/apps/lwiperf/lwiperf.c
+++ b/src/apps/lwiperf/lwiperf.c
@@ -378,6 +378,10 @@ lwiperf_tcp_client_connected(void *arg, struct tcp_pcb *tpcb, err_t err)
   }
   conn->poll_count = 0;
   conn->time_started = sys_now();
+  /* A measurement client must not let Nagle + the peer's delayed ACK pace
+   * one segment per RTT: the board's uplink measured 0.4 Mbit/s with the
+   * socket starved, and the driver's TX queue was empty 20 s out of 20. */
+  tcp_nagle_disable(tpcb);
   return lwiperf_tcp_client_send_more(conn);
 }
 
